From 682c42ea72df32016e4f1881f253ec1127dc7acd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik <erik-131@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 18:28:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/42] NHL: POSIX events hand a signal to the threads already
 waiting; SignalAndWait registers the wait first

Waiters queue on the event: an auto-reset signal goes to the oldest waiter, a manual-reset set releases all of
them even if a reset follows, and SignalAndWait can't lose its wakeup. Same two bugs as rexglue PR 531, written
independently from its description, without nesting the two objects' locks.

---
 src/core/threading_posix.cpp | 177 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 144 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/threading_posix.cpp b/src/core/threading_posix.cpp
